.TH @PROJECT_NAME@ 1 "2026-10-06" "@PROJECT_NAME@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@PROJECT_NAME@ \- package and ports manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @PROJECT_NAME@
.RI [ global-options ]
.I command
.RI [ command-options ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B @PROJECT_NAME@
manages ports, package installation, upgrades, removal, dependency inspection, repositories, and system updates. It uses the configured ports repositories and package database. Operations that modify the system require root privileges.
.PP
Use \fB@PROJECT_NAME@ help\fR to print the built-in command summary.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B search PATTERN
Find ports in the configured repositories.
.TP
.B sync [ARG]
Update the ports database using \fBportsync\fR.
.RS
.TP
.B -p, --prune
Prune local git repositories.
.TP
.B -r, --reset
Reset git repositories.
.RE
.TP
.B build PORT...
Build ports using \fBpkgbuild\fR.
.RS
.TP
.B -f
Force package rebuild.
.TP
.B -m
Skip checksum checking.
.TP
.B -o
Fetch sources only.
.TP
.B -q, --quiet
Show only status messages and errors.
.TP
.B -w
Keep the working directory.
.TP
.B -y
Skip confirmation.
.TP
.B -C, --clean
Remove downloaded sources and prebuilt packages.
.TP
.B --log
Log the build process.
.TP
.B --jobs=N
Override the number of parallel build jobs.
.RE
.TP
.B install PORT...
Build and install ports using \fBpkgbuild\fR.
.RS
.TP
.B -c
Ignore conflicts when installing packages.
.TP
.B -f
Force package rebuild.
.TP
.B -m
Skip checksum checking.
.TP
.B -n
Skip dependencies.
.TP
.B -o
Fetch sources only.
.TP
.B -q, --quiet
Show only status messages and errors.
.TP
.B -r
Reinstall.
.TP
.B -w
Keep the working directory.
.TP
.B -y, --yes
Skip confirmation.
.TP
.B --exclude=LIST
Exclude comma-separated dependencies.
.TP
.B --no-backup
Skip backup when reinstalling packages.
.TP
.B --jobs=N
Override the number of parallel build jobs.
.RE
.TP
.B upgrade PORT...
Upgrade ports using \fBpkgbuild\fR.
.RS
.TP
.B -c
Ignore conflicts when installing packages.
.TP
.B -f
Force package rebuild.
.TP
.B -m
Skip checksum checking.
.TP
.B -n
Skip dependencies.
.TP
.B -o
Fetch sources only.
.TP
.B -q, --quiet
Show only status messages and errors.
.TP
.B -w
Keep the working directory.
.TP
.B -y, --yes
Skip confirmation.
.TP
.B --exclude=LIST
Exclude comma-separated dependencies.
.TP
.B --no-backup
Skip backup when upgrading packages.
.TP
.B --jobs=N
Override the number of parallel build jobs.
.RE
.TP
.B sysup [ARG]
Perform a full system upgrade using \fBpkgbuild\fR while respecting masks.
.RS
.TP
.B -c
Ignore conflicts when installing packages.
.TP
.B -f
Force package rebuild.
.TP
.B -m
Skip checksum checking.
.TP
.B -n
Skip dependencies.
.TP
.B -o
Fetch sources only.
.TP
.B -q, --quiet
Show only status messages and errors.
.TP
.B -w
Keep the working directory.
.TP
.B -y, --yes
Skip confirmation.
.TP
.B --exclude=LIST
Exclude comma-separated dependencies.
.TP
.B --no-backup
Skip backup when upgrading packages.
.TP
.B --jobs=N
Override the number of parallel build jobs.
.RE
.TP
.B remove PORT...
Remove installed ports using \fBpkgdel\fR.
.RS
.TP
.B -y, --yes
Skip confirmation.
.RE
.TP
.B deplist PORT...
Print all dependencies for ports.
.RS
.TP
.B -q, --quick
Skip installed ports.
.TP
.B --exclude=LIST
Exclude comma-separated dependencies.
.RE
.TP
.B redeps PORT...
Find redundant direct dependencies.
.RS
.TP
.B -w, --world
Check redundant entries in the world file.
.TP
.B -f, --fix
Remove redundant port dependencies and world entries. Requires root privileges.
.RE
.TP
.B cache
Clean both the packages and sources caches.
.RS
.TP
.B -p, --pkg
Clean only the packages cache.
.TP
.B -s, --src
Clean only the sources cache.
.RE
.TP
.B cat PORT
Print the port build script.
.TP
.B config
Print the Emerald configuration, repositories, aliases, and masks.
.TP
.B dependent PORT
Print reverse dependencies of a port.
.TP
.B depends PORT
Print direct dependencies of a port.
.TP
.B conflicts PORT
Print ports that conflict with a port.
.TP
.B dup
Print duplicate ports.
.TP
.B files PORT
Print files installed by a port.
.TP
.B foreign
Print installed packages not provided by configured ports.
.TP
.B help
Print built-in help.
.TP
.B hook STAGE ACTION PORT
Run a port hook on demand. Run \fB@PROJECT_NAME@ hook\fR without arguments for hook-specific help.
.TP
.B info PORT
Print port information.
.TP
.B installed
Print all installed ports.
.TP
.B integrity
Check installed port integrity.
.TP
.B is-installed PORT
Check whether a port is installed. The exit status is 0 if installed and 1 otherwise.
.TP
.B locate FILE
Print the location of a file in the ports repository.
.TP
.B alias ARG
Manage aliased ports. Run \fB@PROJECT_NAME@ alias help\fR for usage.
.TP
.B mask ARG
Manage masked ports. Run \fB@PROJECT_NAME@ mask help\fR for usage.
.TP
.B missing-deps
Print missing dependencies.
.TP
.B orphan
Print orphaned installed ports.
.TP
.B outdated
Print installed ports with newer repository versions.
.TP
.B path PORT
Print the path of a port in the repository.
.TP
.B provide FILE
Print ports providing a file.
.TP
.B purge [PORT...]
Remove installed ports and their orphan dependencies.
.TP
.B trigger [PORT...]
Run system post-install triggers.
.TP
.B world [PORT...]
Print, add, or remove entries in the world list.
.TP
.B list
Print all available ports.
.TP
.B version
Print version information and exit.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --append-repo=PATH
Append a custom local repository path. May be used multiple times.
.TP
.B --prepend-repo=PATH
Prepend a custom local repository path. May be used multiple times.
.TP
.B --override-repo=PATH
Override repositories from the repository file with custom local repositories. May be used multiple times.
.TP
.B --repo=PATH
Add a custom repository path for this invocation. May be used multiple times.
.TP
.B --repo-file=FILE
Use FILE as the repository file.
.TP
.B --config-file=FILE
Use FILE as the configuration file.
.TP
.B --alias-file=FILE
Use FILE as the alias file.
.TP
.B --mask-file=FILE
Use FILE as the mask file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @SYSCONFDIR@/@PROJECT_NAME@.conf
Build and runtime configuration.
.TP
.I @SYSCONFDIR@/@PROJECT_NAME@.repo
Repository definitions.
.TP
.I @SYSCONFDIR@/@PROJECT_NAME@.alias
Package aliases.
.TP
.I @SYSCONFDIR@/@PROJECT_NAME@.mask
Ports excluded from system upgrades.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. A non-zero status indicates invalid input, an unavailable port/package, a failed operation, or a detected problem for a checking command.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkgadd (1),
.BR pkgbuild (1),
.BR pkgdel (1),
.BR portsync (1),
.BR revdep (1),
.BR @PROJECT_NAME@.conf (5)
